  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nContinued northwest flow coupled with several mid-level\ndisturbances will contribute to several rounds of light rain and\nsnow showers through Sunday. Continue to favor eastern Finger\nLake locations eastward to the hills south of Syracuse near\nTully into Cortland and Madison counties for any localized\nsnowfall of an inch or two tonight into Sunday morning. Finger\nLake moisture and terrain make these locations favored over\nother spots. Temperatures generally look to remain in the 30's\nto perhaps low 40's through Sunday. \n\nThe 850mb ridge axis does not pass through our area until \nMonday night. Therefore, we remain locked in the cool, cloudy \nnorthwest flow pattern on Monday. Wouldn't be surprised to see \npockets of drizzle lingering into Monday under the thick stratus\ncloud deck. Temperatures remain cool only in the 40's on \nMonday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nFor Tuesday through Saturday: General upper \nlevel ridging remains over the eastern US. There could be a very\nweak disturbance or front passing through toward Friday. \nOtherwise, high pressure looks to remain in control right \nthrough Saturday (if current timing holds). Temperatures will \nsee a gradual warming trend through the week, reaching about 15 \ndegrees above average for daytime highs by Friday and Saturday\n(50's and low 60's). With the generally clear skies and light \nwinds, overnight lows will be on the seasonably cool side, \nmainly in the 30's through the week. Overall a very pleasant \nand fair stretch of late fall weather looks to be in store.",
